{"agent":"pswarm2","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`answer` treats a missing `item` as a wildcard (`not item or m.item == item`) but then relays `item=\"\"` unchanged. Given a pending ask from lane `worker` with `item=\"T-1\"`, `answer(repo, \"worker\", \"use blue\", sender=\"lead\")` succeeds, yet the outbound message has an empty item. The lane is specified to pair and withdraw by item, so the ask stays pending and the same call can be repeated.","digest":"a6bca6a087f6afcd","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/lead.py:answer","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/lead.py:answer"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The lead rollup labels every `IB.pending` row as an \"open ask\" and `answer` accepts any pending message from `to`, with no reason check. A finish/stall wake in that same inbox (`reason=\"merge_offer\"` or `\"message\"`, sender `lane-a`, item `T-9`) is printed as `ask 1. from lane-a about T-9: ...` and `answer(..., to=\"lane-a\", item=\"T-9\")` is allowed even though the lane never asked a question.","digest":"ade5e054d958c469","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/lane_views.py:_lead_text","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lane_views.py:_lead_text"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":11594,"diff_sha":"30536a4c1c33c6762723d5402a98db07f93fc1558bed87293fdecc0f501f006d","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/SW-lead-link","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":113.7,"excluded_bytes":5672,"excluded_files":3,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr"],"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"6d93c49f7e47e4f0","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SW-lead-link.rubber_duck.gro