{"agent":"pswarm2","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`answer` treats a missing `item` as a wildcard: `not item or m.item == item` is true for every pending message from `to`. Given two pending asks from lane `w` (items `T-1` and `T-2`), `answer(repo, \"w\", \"ship it\", sender=\"lead\", item=\"\")` is accepted and the outbound message is stored with `item=\"\"`. The lane is specified to pair and withdraw by `item`, so neither ask is withdrawn, the lead view keeps both as open, and a later call with the same empty item is accepted again.","digest":"4785e3769ed01f84","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/lead.py:answer","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/lead.py:answer"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"Asks are sliced with `asks[:max_asks]` and the empty-slice branch is the same string as “no asks”. Given one pending ask and `max_asks=0` (or any cap that yields no rows), the function does not return early (`asks` is non-empty) and emits `open asks to you: none`, so the lead is told the queue is clear while `pending` still holds the question.","digest":"ff37b46da5fd8a6d","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/lane_views.py:_lead_text","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/api/lane_views.py:_lead_text"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":11594,"diff_sha":"30536a4c1c33c6762723d5402a98db07f93fc1558bed87293fdecc0f501f006d","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/SW-lead-link","diff_stat":{"deletions":13,"files":2,"insertions":17,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":108.6,"excluded_bytes":5672,"excluded_files":3,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr"],"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"9470e650e8f185fc","output_file":".ddflow/local/review