{"agent":"pswarm2","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`answer` treats a missing `item` as a wildcard (`not item or m.item == item`) but then relays `item=\"\"` unchanged. Given a pending ask from lane `worker` with `item=\"T-1\"`, `answer(repo, \"worker\", \"use blue\", sender=\"lead\")` succeeds, yet the outbound message has an empty item. The lane is specified to pair and withdraw by item, so the ask stays pending and the same call can be repeated.","digest":"a6bca6a087f6afcd","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/lead.py:answer","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/lead.py:answer"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The lead rollup labels every `IB.pending` row as an \"open ask\" and `answer` accepts any pending message from `to`, with no reason check. A finish/stall wake in that same inbox (`reason=\"merge_offer\"` or `\"message\"`, sender `lane-a`, item `T-9`) is printed as `ask 1. from lane-a about T-9: ...` and `answer(..., to=\"lane-a\", item=\"T-9\")` is allowed even though the lane never asked a question.","digest":"ade5e054d958c469","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/lane_views.py:_lead_text","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lane_views.py:_lead_text"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"When `max_asks` is 0 and the inbox is non-empty, both branches run: `shown` is forced to `[]`, so `not rows` appends “all N held (lanes.advise_max is 0)” and `len(shown) < len(msgs)` also appends “(N more not shown)”. Input: 3 pending inbox rows and `max_asks=0` yields `your inbox (3): all 3 held (lanes.advise_max is 0) (3 more not shown)` with an empty body, which claims a truncation on top of a zero cap and hides every row the lead would use to steer.","digest":"238d7c711e50ce72","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/lane_views.py:_lead_text","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/api/lane_views.py:_lead_text"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","de