{"agent":"pswarm2","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`answer` treats a missing `item` as a wildcard: `not item or m.item == item` is true for every pending message from `to`. Given two pending asks from lane `w` (items `T-1` and `T-2`), `answer(repo, \"w\", \"ship it\", sender=\"lead\", item=\"\")` is accepted and the outbound message is stored with `item=\"\"`. The lane is specified to pair and withdraw by `item`, so neither ask is withdrawn, the lead view keeps both as open, and a later call with the same empty item is accepted again.","digest":"4785e3769ed01f84","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/lead.py:answer","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/lead.py:answer"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"Asks are sliced with `asks[:max_asks]` and the empty-slice branch is the same string as “no asks”. Given one pending ask and `max_asks=0` (or any cap that yields no rows), the function does not return early (`asks` is non-empty) and emits `open asks to you: none`, so the lead is told the queue is clear while `pending` still holds the question.","digest":"ff37b46da5fd8a6d","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/lane_views.py:_lead_text","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/api/lane_views.py:_lead_text"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":0,"delta_from":"c40d24a2915f74a38e1977be8379685e75dec068","delta_raised":[],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":4482,"diff_sha":"0c616a4e41f8fdc8686b485637f76fca8bbcb25b72e81e6d249b4bd1a73c0154","diff_source":"delta review of 2 commits since c40d24a291","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":113.5,"family":"xai","findings":2,"full_coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"aa27ef0fe23dc5d2","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SW-lead-link.critic.grok-4.7.20261109T230135Z-c916da5f.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"delta","revi